title: Case Manager › Active cases › Tracker of every active case
route: /manager
intro: The tracker is what Active cases opens on, under the folded 'Being prepared' row (and 'Step-down plans' when there are any). It lists the active cases at the sites in view (Both sites: all 56; Site A 33; Site B 23) across every level of care, plus any case signed and sent today. Four tiles count them by status and filter the table when clicked. The table is sorted by what is due next, ten rows a page.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Open Active cases: the tracker is under the folded rows"
screen t0 "Four status tiles in a row\n11 'Needs action' (act today)\n14 'Review due' (review or recertify soon)\n15 'Awaiting payer' (the payer has it)\n16 'On track' (nothing needed)"
process p0 "Tile numbers follow search, level of care and payer\nThey do not follow the status filter, so they always add up to the cases in view"
screen t1 "Table card\nColumns: Case, Status, Next due, Units or days, Level of care, Payer, Approval chance, then a small quick view button and 'Open'\nStatus is the one coloured pill; level of care is plain text; approval chance is one small number\nUnder a case ID, small text when it applies: 'New today', 'Updated for a payer change · 10/20'"
process p1 "Rows are sorted by Next due, soonest first (overdue rows lead)\nTen rows a page, 'Showing 1 to 10 of 56'\nThe header count, the four tiles and this line are one list, so they always agree ('57' with a new case)"
screen t2 "Note under the table\n'Click a row for a quick view, or Open for the full case.'\n'Units or days left are worked out at the usual pace ... Runs out before review appears only when ...'\n'Approval chance estimates how well the paperwork fits the payer's past decisions ... Strong is 80 and above, Moderate 55 to 79, At risk below 55. It never blocks a request.'"

click c1 "Click a tile, for example 'Needs action'"
decision d1 "Was that tile already selected?"
process p2 "Tile gets a green outline\nThe 'Any status' dropdown shows the same status\nTable keeps only that status, and goes back to page 1"
process p3 "Outline goes\nStatus filter is cleared: all cases again"

click c2 "Pick a status in the 'Any status' dropdown"
process p4 "Same effect as clicking that tile"

click c3 "Click a sortable header or 'Previous' / 'Next'"
goto g1 "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › Sort and page the tracker"
process c4 "Look at a row's Status, Units or days and Next due cells"
goto g2 "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › What each tracker cell means"
click c5 "Click its case ID or 'Open'"
goto g3 "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › Open a case from the tracker"
click c6 "Click the row, or its quick view button"
goto g7 "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › Quick view of a case"
goto g8 "Continues in: Case Manager › Sites › What each site sees and out-of-site links"
decision d2 "Does any row match?"
goto g4 "Continues in: Case Manager › Empty states › Nothing to show"
goto g5 "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › A new case joins the tracker"
goto g6 "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › Updated for a payer change"
end e1 "Table shows the matching cases"

s1 --> t0 --> p0 --> t1 --> p1 --> t2
t0 --> c1 --> d1
d1 -->|No| p2
d1 -->|Yes, clicking again| p3
t0 --> c2 --> p4
p2 --> d2
p3 --> d2
p4 --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| e1
d2 -->|No| g4
t1 --> c3 --> g1
t1 --> c4 --> g2
t1 --> c5 --> g3
t1 --> c6 --> g7
t0 -.-> g8
t1 -.-> g5
t1 -.-> g6
